## Spring OXM XXE Vulnerability

**Problem**: Spring's Object/XML mapping (OXM) provides convenient XML marshalling/unmarshalling but inherits XXE vulnerabilities if not explicitly hardened.

**Real incident**: Applications accepting user-uploaded XML configuration files were exploitable via XXE. Attackers could:
- Read application.properties, database credentials, API keys
- Scan internal network via SSRF (check which ports are open)
- Crash service via billion laughs attacks
- Exfiltrate sensitive data without any error messages (blind XXE)

## Vulnerable Implementation

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/config")
public class VulnerableConfigController {

    @Autowired
    private Jaxb2Marshaller jaxb2Marshaller;  // Default = XXE vulnerable

    // VULNERABLE: Default OXM configuration
    @PostMapping("/import")
    public ConfigResponse importConfiguration(@RequestBody String xmlConfig) {
        try {
            AppConfiguration config = (AppConfiguration) 
                jaxb2Marshaller.unmarshal(
                    new StreamSource(new StringReader(xmlConfig))
                );

            // Attacker's XXE payload processed here
            saveConfiguration(config);
            return new ConfigResponse("OK");
        } catch (Exception e) {
            return new ConfigResponse("Error: " + e.getMessage());
        }
    }

    // VULNERABLE: File upload with XML processing
    @PostMapping("/upload")
    public ConfigResponse uploadConfigFile(
            @RequestParam("file") MultipartFile file) throws Exception {

        String xmlContent = new String(file.getBytes());

        // VULNERABLE: No XXE protection on OXM unmarshaller
        AppConfiguration config = (AppConfiguration) 
            jaxb2Marshaller.unmarshal(
                new StreamSource(new StringReader(xmlContent))
            );

        saveConfiguration(config);
        return new ConfigResponse("OK");
    }
}

@Configuration
public class VulnerableOxmConfig {

    @Bean
    public Jaxb2Marshaller jaxb2Marshaller() {
        Jaxb2Marshaller marshaller = new Jaxb2Marshaller();
        marshaller.setClassesToBeBound(AppConfiguration.class);
        // VULNERABLE: No XXE protection configured
        return marshaller;
    }
}
```

**Attack**: User uploads XML with embedded XXE:
```xml
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE foo [
  <!ENTITY xxe SYSTEM "file:///opt/spring-app/application.properties">
]>
<AppConfiguration>
    <name>&xxe;</name>
    <version>1.0</version>
</AppConfiguration>
```

Server parses, expands entity, database credentials exposed.

## Common Mistakes

1. **Blocklist instead of allowlist** — Trying to filter out dangerous characters (like `'`, `--`, `;`) instead of allowlisting expected input patterns. Attackers will always find encoding bypasses (URL encoding, Unicode, double encoding) that evade blocklists.

2. **Sanitizing at the wrong layer** — Applying sanitization in the frontend (JavaScript validation) instead of the backend. Client-side validation is trivially bypassed with curl, Burp Suite, or browser DevTools.

3. **Using string concatenation for queries** — Building queries with template literals or string concatenation instead of parameterized queries. Even "safe" values today can become attack vectors when code changes.

4. **Trusting ORM/framework defaults** — Assuming the ORM automatically prevents injection. Most ORMs have escape hatches (raw queries, text expressions) that bypass parameterization.

## Secure Implementation


### Tier 1: Critical Fix

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/config/v2")
public class SecureConfigController {

    @Autowired
    private Jaxb2Marshaller secureMarshaller;

    private static final long MAX_CONFIG_SIZE = 1_000_000; // 1MB

    @PostMapping("/import")
    public ConfigResponse importConfiguration(
            @RequestBody String xmlConfig) throws Exception {

        // Size validation
        if (xmlConfig.length() > MAX_CONFIG_SIZE) {
            return new ConfigResponse("Error: Configuration too large");
        }

        // XXE validation
        validateNoXxePatterns(xmlConfig);

        try {
            AppConfiguration config = (AppConfiguration) 
                secureMarshaller.unmarshal(
                    new StreamSource(new StringReader(xmlConfig))
                );

            saveConfiguration(config);
            return new ConfigResponse("OK");
        } catch (Exception e) {
            return new ConfigResponse("Error: Configuration invalid");
        }
    }

    private void validateNoXxePatterns(String xml) throws SecurityException {
        if (xml.contains("<!DOCTYPE") || xml.contains("<!ENTITY") || 
            xml.contains("SYSTEM") || xml.contains("PUBLIC")) {
            throw new SecurityException("DOCTYPE/ENTITY declarations not allowed");
        }
    }
}

@Configuration
public class SecureOxmConfig {

    @Bean
    public Jaxb2Marshaller jaxb2Marshaller() {
        Jaxb2Marshaller marshaller = new Jaxb2Marshaller();
        marshaller.setClassesToBeBound(AppConfiguration.class);

        // SECURE: Disable XXE via unmarshaller properties
        Map<String, Object> properties = new HashMap<>();
        properties.put(
            XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_DTD, 
            ""  // Disable external DTD
        );
        properties.put(
            XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_SCHEMA, 
            ""  // Disable external schema
        );
        properties.put(
            "com.sun.org.apache.xerces.impl.Constants.SAX_FEATURE_PREFIX + " +
            "\"features/disallow-doctype-decl\"",
            true  // Reject DOCTYPE
        );

        marshaller.setUnmarshallerProperties(properties);
        return marshaller;
    }

    @Bean
    public DocumentBuilderFactory secureDocumentBuilderFactory() {
        DocumentBuilderFactory dbf = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();

        try {
            // Disable DTD entirely
            dbf.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/disallow-doctype-decl", true);

            // Disable external entities
            dbf.setFeature("http://xml.org/sax/features/external-general-entities", false);
            dbf.setFeature("http://xml.org/sax/features/external-parameter-entities", false);
            dbf.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/nonvalidating/load-external-dtd", false);

            // Disable XXE via XMLConstants
            dbf.setAttribute(XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_DTD, "");
            dbf.setAttribute(XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_SCHEMA, "");

            // Disable entity expansion
            dbf.setXIncludeAware(false);
            dbf.setExpandEntityReferences(false);
        } catch (ParserConfigurationException e) {
            // Log and continue with defaults
        }

        return dbf;
    }
}

// Input validation filter
@Component
public class XmlSecurityFilter implements Filter {

    private static final List<String> BLOCKED_PATTERNS = Arrays.asList(
        "<!DOCTYPE",
        "<!ENTITY",
        "SYSTEM ",
        "PUBLIC ",
        "file://",
        "jar:",
        "netdoc:"
    );

    @Override
    public void doFilter(ServletRequest request, ServletResponse response,
                        FilterChain chain) throws IOException, ServletException {

        HttpServletRequest httpRequest = (HttpServletRequest) request;

        if ("POST".equalsIgnoreCase(httpRequest.getMethod()) &&
            httpRequest.getContentType() != null &&
            httpRequest.getContentType().contains("xml")) {

            // Wrap request to capture body
            CachedBodyHttpServletRequest cachedRequest = 
                new CachedBodyHttpServletRequest(httpRequest);

            String body = cachedRequest.getBody();

            // Check for XXE patterns
            for (String pattern : BLOCKED_PATTERNS) {
                if (body.toUpperCase().contains(pattern.toUpperCase())) {
                    ((HttpServletResponse) response).setStatus(400);
                    response.getWriter().write("Invalid XML format");
                    return;
                }
            }

            chain.doFilter(cachedRequest, response);
        } else {
            chain.doFilter(request, response);
        }
    }
}
```

