## Validation and Legacy System Handling

**Health check for XXE protections:**

```java
@Component
public class XxeSecurityValidator {

    public boolean validateXxeProtection() {
        try {
            // Try to parse XXE payload—should fail
            String xxePayload = "<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>" +
                "<!DOCTYPE foo [" +
                "  <!ENTITY xxe SYSTEM \"file:///etc/passwd\">" +
                "]>" +
                "<test>&xxe;</test>";

            DocumentBuilderFactory dbf = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
            dbf.setFeature("http://apache.org/xml/features/disallow-doctype-decl", true);
            dbf.setFeature("http://xml.org/sax/features/external-general-entities", false);

            try {
                dbf.newDocumentBuilder().parse(
                    new InputSource(new StringReader(xxePayload))
                );
                // If we get here without exception, XXE protection failed
                return false;
            } catch (SAXParseException e) {
                // Expected—XXE protection is working
                return true;
            }
        } catch (Exception e) {
            return false;
        }
    }
}

@RestController
public class HealthController {

    @Autowired
    private XxeSecurityValidator validator;

    @GetMapping("/health/xxe-protection")
    public ResponseEntity<?> checkXxeProtection() {
        if (validator.validateXxeProtection()) {
            return ResponseEntity.ok("XXE protections active");
        } else {
            return ResponseEntity.status(500).body("XXE protections failed");
        }
    }
}
```

**Legacy system with controlled external DTD loading:**

```java
@Configuration
public class LegacyXmlConfig {

    private static final Set<String> ALLOWED_DTDS = Set.of(
        "http://internal-dtd-server/schemas/v1.dtd",
        "http://internal-dtd-server/schemas/v2.dtd"
    );

    @Bean("legacyMarshaller")
    public Jaxb2Marshaller legacyMarshaller() {
        Jaxb2Marshaller marshaller = new Jaxb2Marshaller();
        marshaller.setClassesToBeBound(LegacyConfig.class);

        // Allow ONLY specific DTDs from trusted internal server
        Map<String, Object> properties = new HashMap<>();
        properties.put(
            XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_DTD,
            "http://internal-dtd-server"  // Only allow this domain
        );
        properties.put(
            XMLConstants.ACCESS_EXTERNAL_SCHEMA,
            "http://internal-dtd-server"
        );

        marshaller.setUnmarshallerProperties(properties);
        return marshaller;
    }
}

@RestController
@RequestMapping("/legacy")
public class LegacyConfigController {

    @Autowired
    @Qualifier("legacyMarshaller")
    private Jaxb2Marshaller legacyMarshaller;

    @PostMapping("/import")
    public ConfigResponse importLegacyConfig(@RequestBody String xml) {
        try {
            // Validate that DOCTYPE references only allowed DTDs
            if (!isAllowedDtd(xml)) {
                return new ConfigResponse("Error: DTD not in approved list");
            }

            LegacyConfig config = (LegacyConfig) 
                legacyMarshaller.unmarshal(
                    new StreamSource(new StringReader(xml))
                );

            return new ConfigResponse("OK");
        } catch (Exception e) {
            return new ConfigResponse("Error: Processing failed");
        }
    }

    private boolean isAllowedDtd(String xml) {
        // Extract DTD reference
        Pattern pattern = Pattern.compile(
            "<!DOCTYPE.*SYSTEM\s+\"([^\"]+)\""
        );
        Matcher matcher = pattern.matcher(xml);

        if (matcher.find()) {
            String dtdUrl = matcher.group(1);
            return ALLOWED_DTDS.contains(dtdUrl);
        }

        // No DTD reference is also OK
        return true;
    }
}
```

**Key points for legacy systems:**
- Only allow external DTDs from specific trusted internal servers
- Validate DTD URLs against whitelist before processing
- Use network isolation (firewall rules) to block unexpected outbound connections
- Log all DTD loading attempts
- Plan migration to modern XML processing without external DTDs


